WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.179 --> 00:00:01.179
Careful!

00:00:01.179 --> 00:00:02.640
This video contains manga spoilers!

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:08.090
The moment the 8 year old Momo sacrificed
his childhood to transform into a full grown

00:00:08.090 --> 00:00:13.470
dragon and face his greatest fears head on
in order to save his country, I knew that

00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:26.900
we had just witnessed the climax of one of
the best character arcs in the One Piece.

00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:33.410
What an incredible turnaround for the traumatized
and mistrusting little kid Luffy found in

00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:38.700
the depths of Punk Hazard, whom he then turned
into a full-fledged leader in a matter of

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:39.700
months.

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:44.570
Being able to hear the voices of all thing,
he does not only posses one of the rarest

00:00:44.570 --> 00:00:50.100
powers in the story, but his ability to command
the titanic elephant Zunesha suggests that

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:56.410
he holds even greater power still, all on
top of a ridiculously mighty devil fruit.

00:00:56.410 --> 00:01:10.040
And I'll even go so far and claim that the
annoyingly perverted side of Momo, that made

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:15.970
me dislike the boy from the very start, was
written on purpose by Oda to give us the most

00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:19.430
satisfying development we can get as a reader.

00:01:19.430 --> 00:01:21.860
From hate to love.

00:01:21.860 --> 00:01:26.271
Because over the course of Wano, Momo has
gained more and more of my respect, and I

00:01:26.271 --> 00:01:30.670
can now say that I absolutely love his character.

00:01:30.670 --> 00:01:35.369
Which is good, because I've long been subscribed
to the idea that Momo is set up to be one

00:01:35.369 --> 00:01:38.520
of the most important characters in the story.

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:40.159
You know, just like you should be to this
channel.

00:01:40.159 --> 00:01:47.110
Okay so let's start by addressing the biggest
criticism people have for Momo: His pervertedness.

00:01:47.110 --> 00:01:52.079
Which is great, because it's coincidentally
the the secret ingredient to the success of

00:01:52.079 --> 00:01:54.890
his character arc.

00:01:54.890 --> 00:02:03.390
And you might be thinking now, that I'm giving
Oda too much credit here, and maybe I am,

00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:05.410
but hear me out:

00:02:05.410 --> 00:02:09.779
Momo's perverted nature differs from that
of Sanji or Brook, which for some people muddies

00:02:09.779 --> 00:02:16.200
these otherwise fantastic characters, in that
A, this is a little kid and B, he actually

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:20.560
does the things that Brook and Sanji would
love to, but never could.

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:25.870
This is important, because for Sanji and brook,
Oda clearly thinks it's a funny character

00:02:25.870 --> 00:02:31.489
quirk and the fact that Sanji's peep attempts
always end in violence, is supposed to make

00:02:31.489 --> 00:02:42.099
it a likable quirk I believe, even if for
some it isn't.

00:02:42.099 --> 00:02:47.189
With Momo on the other hand, the smugness
with which he uses his young age to do what

00:02:47.189 --> 00:02:52.949
he does, even from Oda's perspective, is clearly
meant to piss you off.

00:02:52.949 --> 00:02:58.830
Even if you have no problem with Sanji and
Brook and find their perkiness hilarious,

00:02:58.830 --> 00:03:01.780
Momo would annoy you for his smugness.

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:07.580
So in my eyes, this is clearly a trait that
is meant to give us a false first impression

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:08.870
of Momo.

00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:14.650
I think Momo actually got this quirk mostly
from the people he grew up with, Kinemon,

00:03:14.650 --> 00:03:27.689
Oden, Rayleigh who all are infamous for their
love of women.

00:03:27.689 --> 00:03:32.620
When Yamato sticks him inside her shirt to
protect him, he actually doesn't think anything

00:03:32.620 --> 00:03:38.189
pervy at all, fully in the process of accepting
his uselessness and preparing to grow as a

00:03:38.189 --> 00:03:39.189
character.

00:03:39.189 --> 00:03:44.129
The truth here is, that Oda wanted you and
me to dislike Momo from the start, seeing

00:03:44.129 --> 00:03:49.260
him as a perverted, spoiled and useless kid,
holding everyone back.

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:55.099
Because his change as a character would be
so much more drastic.

00:03:55.099 --> 00:04:00.369
I don't want to exonerate him completely here,
I'm sure he genuinely loves those boobs, but

00:04:00.369 --> 00:04:06.359
I also think it's important to consider that
this is an 8 year old who just lost both his

00:04:06.359 --> 00:04:12.359
parents as well as his sister mere days ago
and is terribly traumatized when we first

00:04:12.359 --> 00:04:15.469
meet him, only we don't know that yet of course.

00:04:15.469 --> 00:04:20.159
And so, when he gets to b bath and sleep in
the same bed with Nami and Robin, I think

00:04:20.159 --> 00:04:26.370
this is actually Momo looking for some much
needed motherly love rather than anything

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:27.370
else.

00:04:27.370 --> 00:04:32.550
What makes Momo's arc so special in retrospect,
not only in One Piece, but in storytelling

00:04:32.550 --> 00:04:38.360
overall, is that his development breaks with
two very established tropes.

00:04:38.360 --> 00:04:45.889
The typical hero slash shounen arcs are A
that from Boy to man or B that from man to

00:04:45.889 --> 00:04:46.979
leader.

00:04:46.979 --> 00:04:51.800
Boy to man actually has nothing to do with
age per se, but simply means that a character

00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:56.980
needs to leave the nest, question their naive
ideas and learn to face the real world.

00:04:56.980 --> 00:04:59.509
Basically a coming of age story.

00:04:59.509 --> 00:05:10.539
Usopp falls really nicely into that trope.

00:05:10.539 --> 00:05:15.020
The arc from man to leader leader on the other
hand, means that a character goes form being

00:05:15.020 --> 00:05:20.800
concerned only for finding a path for himself,
to realizing that he must help others finding

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:21.849
their way as well.

00:05:21.849 --> 00:05:32.510
Zoro snd Sanji are great examples of this.

00:05:32.510 --> 00:05:37.520
And since I guess you're curious, Luffy's
arc is that from Leader to visionary, going

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:53.050
from helping a few others find the right path
to changing a whole society.

00:05:53.050 --> 00:06:04.030
I always loved how these storytelling best
practices explain why One Piece works so wonderfully.

00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:09.139
Luffy has the most important arc, but all
other straw hats have their own protagonist

00:06:09.139 --> 00:06:10.139
story as well.

00:06:10.139 --> 00:06:13.870
Now, you might have already figured out what
makes Momo an odd one out here.

00:06:13.870 --> 00:06:21.229
His character arc basically forces him to
combine A and B to go from boy directly to

00:06:21.229 --> 00:06:22.590
being a leader.

00:06:22.590 --> 00:06:28.770
Momo, despite being a normal kid, is suffocating
under the expectations of an entire oppressed

00:06:28.770 --> 00:06:35.330
nation to become the same great leader that
his father used to be, before being executed

00:06:35.330 --> 00:06:49.090
days before meeting Luffy.

00:06:49.090 --> 00:06:50.529
Talk about a tough spot to be in.

00:06:50.529 --> 00:06:56.961
He is still too young to become a man and
far from being the natural leader Luffy is.

00:06:56.961 --> 00:07:04.529
And this gives Momo the ultimate arc, to work
his ass off to go through not just one, but

00:07:04.529 --> 00:07:10.909
two character changes, way faster and at a
way younger age than most other characters

00:07:10.909 --> 00:07:12.069
in One Piece.

00:07:12.069 --> 00:07:17.969
And so, once I had the full set of information
available to me in Wano, Momo's arc became

00:07:17.969 --> 00:07:21.220
a lot more apparent and interesting.

00:07:21.220 --> 00:07:26.509
After losing his parents and being sent into
the future, on top of everything else, he

00:07:26.509 --> 00:07:31.650
also gets separated from the only three people
that accompanied him at this point, making

00:07:31.650 --> 00:07:41.669
Kanjuro's betrayal the more impactful later
on.

00:07:41.669 --> 00:07:47.569
He then survive alone on Punk hazard, with
no time to mourn his dead parents and terrible

00:07:47.569 --> 00:07:49.039
fate.

00:07:49.039 --> 00:07:54.409
When taken in by the straw hats, he is initially
very distrusting, only revealing his true

00:07:54.409 --> 00:08:00.360
identity on Zou after having slowly warming
up to the crew's kindness as well as their

00:08:00.360 --> 00:08:02.949
strength.

00:08:02.949 --> 00:08:14.150
While he always tries to live according to
all the expectations put on his shoulders,

00:08:14.150 --> 00:08:22.349
up until Zou, he basically is a still a traumatized
kid always put in bubble wrap by the retainers.

00:08:22.349 --> 00:08:26.479
On Zou, he has his first real moment of character
growth.

00:08:26.479 --> 00:08:35.779
After revealing his true identity, he tries
to assume the role of leader, but fails.

00:08:35.779 --> 00:08:44.850
[...] Luffy again is the one to teach him
an important lesson in true leadership here.

00:08:44.850 --> 00:08:50.310
And so Momo understands what he needs to do
in order to form the big alliance to take

00:08:50.310 --> 00:08:52.990
down Kaido and save his country.

00:08:52.990 --> 00:08:57.850
Being a leader means being the servant of
your people and not the other way around.

00:08:57.850 --> 00:09:04.120
I was also very impressed by the way he handled
Zunesha a bit later, even though suddenly

00:09:04.120 --> 00:09:09.510
having a depressed ancient giant elephant
talking to you in your, understandably might

00:09:09.510 --> 00:09:18.050
come as a shock for an 8 year old.

00:09:18.050 --> 00:09:20.010
Bravo momo.

00:09:20.010 --> 00:09:26.120
Now it is on Wano and more specifically Onishima
however, where Momo's arc now comes to full

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:27.360
bloom for me.

00:09:27.360 --> 00:09:33.940
At first, it was clear to me, that reaching
his home and facing the aftermath of all the

00:09:33.940 --> 00:09:38.650
horrors he had to live through here, was overwhelming
for Momo.

00:09:38.650 --> 00:09:43.350
Now that it is actually time for him to assume
his position as leader, he quickly comes to

00:09:43.350 --> 00:09:48.220
terms with the fact that he is not the person
everyone wants him to be.

00:09:48.220 --> 00:10:00.260
The son of the endlessly charismatic and powerful
Oden.

00:10:00.260 --> 00:10:06.460
Momo sinks into self-doubt and leaves most
of the decision making to Luffy and the scabbards.

00:10:06.460 --> 00:10:12.360
He feels helplessly pushed around by the events
unfolding throughout the country.

00:10:12.360 --> 00:10:16.199
It takes a real shock for momo to come out
of his stupor.

00:10:16.199 --> 00:10:22.180
And it is the three most scary events in Wano
so far, that bring out the best in him.

00:10:22.180 --> 00:10:27.839
First, he is betrayed and taken Hostage by
Kanjuro, one of the people he had trusted

00:10:27.839 --> 00:10:38.399
the most.

00:10:38.399 --> 00:10:44.060
And still, instead of feeling defeated, he
starts to fight himself for the first time.

00:10:44.060 --> 00:10:56.649
Next, he gets put on a crucifix in front of
the man that killed his father.

00:10:56.649 --> 00:11:02.649
And given the option to save his own live,
as a fucking 8 year old kid, he decides to

00:11:02.649 --> 00:11:09.529
die for his beliefs and declares himself shogun
anyway, securing him the immediate respect

00:11:09.529 --> 00:11:11.529
of all his followers.

00:11:11.529 --> 00:11:16.121
Finally, after learning the important role
he has to play from his fathers diary, he

00:11:16.121 --> 00:11:21.060
is faced with the prospect of Onigashima crashing
into the flower capital.

00:11:21.060 --> 00:11:27.639
And reaching the climax of his arc, he decides
to sacrifice 20 years of his life and his

00:11:27.639 --> 00:11:32.850
remaining childhood, and orders Shinobu to
age him to 28.

00:11:32.850 --> 00:11:40.639
Another really important moment, as he doesn't
take the scabbards wanting to protect him

00:11:40.639 --> 00:11:42.130
as an excuse anymore.

00:11:42.130 --> 00:11:47.259
What made this so emotional for me, was that
Momo knows fully well, that this won't change

00:11:47.259 --> 00:11:55.579
the fact that he's 8 years at heart, but it
gave him the chance to fight and make a difference.

00:11:55.579 --> 00:11:57.930
Flying up and dealing with the problem himself.

00:11:57.930 --> 00:12:04.259
The boy has the courage to face all his fears
at once: Heights, Kaido, the responsibility

00:12:04.259 --> 00:12:08.360
to lead, and he passes with flying colors.

00:12:08.360 --> 00:12:13.079
Watching Luffy has taught him the most important
lesson of all.

00:12:13.079 --> 00:12:18.470
You have to take responsibility for what happens
to you, otherwise you will never be able to

00:12:18.470 --> 00:12:20.149
change anything.

00:12:20.149 --> 00:12:24.699
And so it is actually not surprising that
he not only takes the form of the two men

00:12:24.699 --> 00:12:27.800
under whose shadow he had to live until now.

00:12:27.800 --> 00:12:34.460
Kaido as a dragon and Oden as a man, finally
prepared to assume his role and surpass them

00:12:34.460 --> 00:12:35.839
both as leaders.

00:12:35.839 --> 00:12:42.339
Given all of his powers, and whatever is written
about him in his fathers diary, Momo is bound

00:12:42.339 --> 00:12:46.149
to be one of the decisive characters once
we reach the end game.

00:12:46.149 --> 00:12:51.680
His inspiration after all is Momotaro, the
hero, who got accompanied by a monkey, Luffy,

00:12:51.680 --> 00:12:59.860
a dog, Yamato and a pheasant, possibly Aokiji.

00:12:59.860 --> 00:13:04.519
All YOU need to understand, is why Luffy was
the only one who could have turned this 8

00:13:04.519 --> 00:13:08.910
year old traumatized kid into the next Shogun
of Wano.

00:13:08.910 --> 00:13:15.430
And this video will tell exactly why.

